<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CspTrustedSite xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        FIRST CspTrustedSite IN THIS REPO. Field list confirmed empirically on 2026-08-30 by a
        Tooling API describe of the CspTrustedSite object against usman-dpeg (the
        salesforce-api-context MCP is not configured in .mcp.json, so the org is the schema source
        of truth — .claude/rules/salesforce-global-rule.md constraint 3 fallback).

        ⚠ NOTE WHAT IS ABSENT: there is no isApplicableToScriptSrc element. script-src is what a
        CSP Trusted Site grants BY DEFAULT; the booleans below only ADD further directives. Do not
        go looking for a script-src flag and do not invent one.

        ═══ WHY THESE TWO DIRECTIVES AND NOT THE OTHERS ═══
        Cloudflare's own CSP reference requires exactly two:
            script-src  https://challenges.cloudflare.com   (implicit — see above)
            frame-src   https://challenges.cloudflare.com   (isApplicableToFrameSrc, below)
        The widget is an IFRAME served from challenges.cloudflare.com, so without frame-src the
        api.js script loads and then renders nothing — a blank space where the checkbox should be,
        with a console error and no Apex-side symptom at all.
        connect-src is enabled because the widget's challenge platform issues fetch/XHR calls back
        to the same host while solving. img-src, style-src, font-src and media-src are left FALSE:
        Turnstile's visual assets are inside its own iframe, which carries its own origin and its
        own CSP, so granting them on the parent document buys nothing and widens the surface.
        Camera and microphone are not requested; CanAccessCamera/CanAccessMicrophone exist on the
        object and are deliberately omitted.

        ═══ 🔴 THIS FILE IS NECESSARY AND NOT SUFFICIENT. GATE C. ═══
        The DPEG Broker Portal is an LWR Experience site, and an LWR site ALSO has its own
        "Security & Privacy" CSP level in Experience Builder. That setting lives in the networks/
        and sites/ trees, which .forceignore excludes ENTIRELY (lines 509-522), so it cannot be
        deployed from this repo and cannot be verified from source — the same class of trap as the
        settings/** one already recorded against this project: a force-ignored tree never
        reconciles, so a repo file describing it would be unverified fiction.
        Relaxing it is therefore a MANUAL, POST-DEPLOY step owned by the portal administrator, and
        it is written up in docs/runbooks/2026-08-30-turnstile-post-deploy.md.
        🔴 ACCEPTANCE FOR THIS COMPONENT IS A BROWSER CHECK ON THE LIVE GUEST PAGE — the widget
        must actually render and be solvable for an anonymous visitor. A green deploy of this file
        proves only that the record exists.

        Context is All rather than Communities so that the same trusted site also covers any
        internal LEX preview of the component during troubleshooting; the endpoint is a single
        first-party-to-Cloudflare host with no wildcard, so the wider context costs nothing.
    -->
    <context>All</context>
    <description>Cloudflare Turnstile CAPTCHA on the public DPEG Broker Portal. Grants script-src (implicit) plus frame-src and connect-src. NOT sufficient alone - the LWR site CSP level is a manual Experience Builder step. See ARCHITECTURE.md 3.5.</description>
    <endpointUrl>https://challenges.cloudflare.com</endpointUrl>
    <isActive>true</isActive>
    <isApplicableToConnectSrc>true</isApplicableToConnectSrc>
    <isApplicableToFontSrc>false</isApplicableToFontSrc>
    <isApplicableToFrameSrc>true</isApplicableToFrameSrc>
    <isApplicableToImgSrc>false</isApplicableToImgSrc>
    <isApplicableToMediaSrc>false</isApplicableToMediaSrc>
    <isApplicableToStyleSrc>false</isApplicableToStyleSrc>
</CspTrustedSite>
